# {{given name|en|male|from=Hebrew}}, English form of [[Jeremiah]]. Also used to anglicize Irish [[Diarmaid]] ([[Dermot]]).
#* {{RQ:KJV|Matthew|2|17|text=Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by '''Jeremy''' the prophet.}}
#* '''1840''' John Bowring: ''Memoirs of Jeremy Bentham. Tait's Edinburgh Magazine, p.169'':
#*: He had the name of '''Jeremy''' given to him, because Jeremiah, as his father said, was a family name; and there was an advantage in curtailing a syllable, and in showing a preference towards the names of the New Testament over those of the old.
#* '''2004 October 22''', ''{{w|QI}}'', Season 2, Episode 4:
#*: ''{{w|Stephen Fry|Fry}}'': You don't meet many American '''Jeremies''', do you? Have you ever met an American '''Jeremy'''?<br>''{{w|Jeremy Clarkson|Clarkson}}'': No, it's too complicated. There's three syllables.

